---
title: Year end
description: The Year end step in the last quarter of a financial year.
sidebar:
  order: 13
---

In the last quarter of a financial year, the step bar has a fifth step, **Year end**. It works on the financial year that ends in this quarter.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/year-end-overview" caption="The Year end step." /%}

## Order of work

{% steps %}

1. **Complete the quarter** under **Review › Complete**. Completing the last quarter of a financial year locks the books to the quarter end and keeps the case open for the year-end work.
2. **Year-end adjustments** are recorded under step 3 in the year-end adjustment window after the quarter is complete.
3. **Year close.** A manager closes the financial year. The close checks that the entries needing review are approved, that every bank account is reconciled at the year end, that the subledgers agree with the general ledger and that the suspense account is clear. It then stores a snapshot of the figures.
4. **Deliverables.** The financial statements, the AGM documents, the tax computation and Form C-S are prepared after the close.
5. **Case completion.** The case owner, or a manager, selects **Mark case complete** with a note on the completed work.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="note" %}
This chapter gives an overview only. Detailed instructions for each year-end task will be added in a later edition.
{% /aside %}
